@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+---
+name: office-docx
+description: Create, read, edit, and validate Word documents (.docx).
+---
+
+# Word documents
+
+Follow explicit user or workspace requirements for an environment or library. Otherwise call `load_workspace_dependencies`, run its `node` executable, and import the absolute `officeLibraries` path with `pathToFileURL`. This module provides `docx`, `readOfficePackage`, `DOMParser`, and `XMLSerializer`. Do not install packages or discover a system interpreter. If the module is unavailable, report the missing resource rather than using another environment silently.
+
+Keep task scripts and deliverables in the workspace; the runtime and skill directories are read-only. Match the requested language and preserve an existing document's design. Save a new file unless an in-place edit is requested.
+
+## Create and edit
+
+Use `docx` for new documents, including paragraphs, text runs, styles, tables, images, headers, footers, and sections. For example, in a task `.mjs` script run with the returned Node:
+
+```js
+import { writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';
+import { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';
+const { docx } = await import(pathToFileURL(process.argv[2]).href);
+const { Document, Packer, Paragraph, TextRun, HeadingLevel } = docx;
+const document = new Document({ sections: [{ children: [
+  new Paragraph({ text: 'Project report', heading: HeadingLevel.TITLE }),
+  new Paragraph({ children: [new TextRun('The requested findings go here.')] }),
+] }] });
+await writeFile('report.docx', await Packer.toBuffer(document));
+```
+
+The `docx` creation API does not read arbitrary existing documents. For existing files, use `readOfficePackage(await readFile(path))`; inspect only the affected part through `pkg.xml('word/document.xml')`, then change the relevant WordprocessingML text nodes or properties. Find nodes by namespace URI, not an assumed prefix. A title can be an ordinary paragraph. Preserve its runs and formatting; replacing the whole paragraph's text destroys mixed formatting. For a replacement spanning runs, distribute the new text across the intended run nodes and preserve their properties. Require an unambiguous target before changing it.
+
+Call `pkg.replaceXml(partName, document)` only for modified parts, then `await writeFile(output, await pkg.save())`. `pkg.names()` lists package members, `pkg.part(name)` returns copied current bytes, and `pkg.xml(name)` returns a detached XML document. For new images or other parts, `pkg.setPart(name, bytes)` adds or replaces bytes and `pkg.deletePart(name)` removes a part; update content types and relationships together. Untouched parts, including drawings, relationships, comments, and unsupported extensions, retain their original bytes. ZIP metadata and digital signatures are not preserved. XML editing is not tracked-change authoring: do not present ordinary replacements, colored text, or comments as real revisions. For actual revisions, modify and verify the relevant revision structures explicitly.
+
+Use heading/body styles and section-aware table widths, including merged cells and nested tables. Set CJK run fonts through the appropriate East Asian font property; an available font name alone does not establish rendered glyphs.
+
+## Check and deliver
+
+Reopen saved bytes with `readOfficePackage` and verify requested content, formatting, and required unchanged content. This does not paginate or render. Load `office-render` for requested images or visual inspection and for appearance-focused changes to fonts, colors, spacing, sizing, or alignment unless the user explicitly skips rendering. New files and content edits with incidental formatting need no render by themselves. Load `office-export-pdf` for PDF output.
+
+Deliver the final DOCX through `present` when available, keeping the actual file in place. Otherwise use the session's supported file delivery method. Do not deliver temporary QA files unless requested.
