@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+---
+name: office-pptx
+description: Create, read, edit, and validate PowerPoint presentations (.pptx).
+---
+
+# PowerPoint presentations
+
+Honor explicit user or workspace requirements. Otherwise call `load_workspace_dependencies`, run its `node` executable and import its absolute `officeLibraries` path with `pathToFileURL`. The module exports `PptxGenJS`, `readOfficePackage`, `DOMParser`, and `XMLSerializer`. Do not install packages or discover another interpreter. Report missing resources when they prevent the operation.
+
+Keep scripts and outputs in the task workspace; shared runtime and skill directories are read-only. Match the requested language and preserve the existing deck's design. Save a new file unless an in-place edit is requested.
+
+## Create and edit
+
+Use `PptxGenJS` for new editable slides, text runs, tables, images, charts, slide masters and notes. Use local images. Positions and sizes use inches; text sizes use points. Set page dimensions and chart data explicitly:
+
+```js
+import { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';
+const { PptxGenJS } = await import(pathToFileURL(process.argv[2]).href);
+const deck = new PptxGenJS();
+deck.layout = 'LAYOUT_WIDE';
+const slide = deck.addSlide();
+slide.addText('Quarterly report', { x: 0.6, y: 0.4, w: 12, h: 0.8, fontSize: 30 });
+slide.addChart(deck.ChartType.bar,
+  [{ name: 'Revenue', labels: ['Q1', 'Q2'], values: [12, 18] }],
+  { x: 0.8, y: 1.6, w: 11.5, h: 4.8, catAxisLabelFontSize: 16 });
+await deck.writeFile({ fileName: 'report.pptx' });
+```
+
+PptxGenJS creates presentations; it does not import existing ones. For edits, open original bytes with `readOfficePackage(await readFile(path))`. Inspect the presentation's slide relationships and affected slide, layout, shape, text-run, table, chart or notes XML. Use namespace-aware XML traversal with `pkg.xml(partName)`. Preserve text-run properties, shape geometry, relationships, and unknown extensions; do not rebuild the deck to perform a targeted edit. Require an unambiguous target before mutation.
+
+For a title in the first slide, locate its shape and DrawingML text runs in the actual slide part; update only the intended text nodes. For a title centered on a slide, both paragraph alignment and shape geometry must be centered against the slide width. Inspect and change both, then verify them after saving.
+
+Write each modified document back with `pkg.replaceXml(partName, document)` and save once with `await writeFile(output, await pkg.save())`. `pkg.part(name)` supplies original bytes for embedded resources. Untouched parts retain their original bytes, including animations, SmartArt, charts and embedded workbooks. Native chart edits must update and verify both chart caches and the embedded workbook; changing only visible labels or a chart cache is incomplete. Modifying notes requires updating their corresponding notes parts.
+
+## Check and deliver
+
+Reopen the saved package to verify slide count, requested text, formatting, geometry, chart data, notes and required unchanged parts. Check the native chart's embedded workbook. Package inspection does not establish text fit, contrast or rendering fidelity.
+
+Load `office-render` for requested images or visual inspection and appearance-focused styling, spacing, sizing, or alignment changes unless the user skips rendering. New content with incidental formatting does not itself require rendering. Load `office-export-pdf` for PDF output. Deliver the final PPTX with `present` when available, keeping that file in place; otherwise use the session's supported delivery method. Leave intermediate reports out of delivery unless requested.
