@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+---
+name: office-xlsx
+description: Read, create, edit, and validate Excel workbooks, data, and formulas (.xlsx).
+---
+
+# Excel workbooks
+
+Honor explicit user or workspace requirements. Otherwise call `load_workspace_dependencies`, run its `node` executable, and import the absolute `officeLibraries` path with `pathToFileURL`. The module exports `ExcelJS`, the `aq` Arquero table API, and `readOfficePackage`. Do not install packages or discover another interpreter. Report missing resources when they prevent the operation.
+
+Keep scripts and outputs in the task workspace; shared runtime and skill directories are read-only. Save a new file unless an in-place edit is requested.
+
+## Read and modify
+
+Use ExcelJS to read workbook values, formulas, styles and cell types and to create new workbooks. Arquero provides table transformations and aggregations for analysis. A data table is not a workbook: exporting a table over an existing file loses workbook features. Write only the intended ranges.
+
+For a new workbook:
+
+```js
+import { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';
+const { ExcelJS } = await import(pathToFileURL(process.argv[2]).href);
+const workbook = new ExcelJS.Workbook();
+const sheet = workbook.addWorksheet('Revenue');
+sheet.addRows([['Quarter', 'Revenue'], ['Q1', 12], ['Q2', 18],
+  ['Total', { formula: 'SUM(B2:B3)' }]]);
+sheet.getRow(1).font = { bold: true };
+sheet.columns.forEach(column => { column.width = 18; });
+await workbook.xlsx.writeFile('report.xlsx');
+```
+
+ExcelJS does not preserve every existing workbook feature when writing, including charts and some extensions. For existing files, use `readOfficePackage(await readFile(path))` and make targeted OOXML edits instead of an ExcelJS read/write round trip. Inspect workbook relationships to resolve sheet names to parts; do not assume the first sheet is `sheet1.xml`. Check affected cell types, formulas, styles, merged ranges and referenced ranges before changing anything.
+
+`pkg.xml(partName)` returns a detached XML document. Locate worksheet cells by their `r` coordinate and namespace URI; preserve row/cell ordering and style references. Cells can refer to shared strings or contain inline text, typed values, or formulas. A shared string can be used by multiple cells: do not modify a shared-string entry when only one cell should change. Use a dedicated or inline string for that cell. Preserve numeric values, booleans, dates and identifiers as intended types; number formatting does not convert types.
+
+For formula edits, preserve the `<f>` expression, remove stale cached `<v>` values and invalidate relevant calculation-chain information so recalculation can rebuild it. Never describe an absent/stale cache as a calculated result. Use `pkg.replaceXml` only for modified parts and `await writeFile(output, await pkg.save())` once. Untouched parts, including charts, macros and relationships, retain their original bytes. Preserve the original and verify any advanced feature explicitly. Do not rename XLS/XLSB/encrypted files to XLSX.
+
+Writing a formula does not calculate it. ExcelJS and Arquero are not Excel formula engines. When fresh results are required, load `office-recalculate`; do not replace requested formulas with constants.
+
+## Check and deliver
+
+Reopen saved bytes and verify sheet names, values, cell types, formulas, styles and totals against source data, including required unchanged content. Load `office-render` for requested visual inspection or appearance-focused changes to fills, alignment, spacing or sizing unless the user skips rendering. New workbooks, data and formula edits do not require rendering solely for incidental bold headers or number formats.
+
+Load `office-recalculate` for refreshed formula results and `office-export-pdf` for PDF output. Deliver the verified workbook with `present` when available, keeping the actual file in place; otherwise use the session's supported delivery method. Omit temporary reports unless requested.
